{"name":"Supernatural","hex":"#313641","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"supernatural","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Above nature; beyond or added to nature, often so considered because it is given by a deity or some force beyond that with which humans are born.","Not of the usual; not natural; altered by forces that are not understood fully, if at all."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being","Supernatural beings and events collectively"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supernatural"}],"entries":[{"title":"Supernatural","blocks":[{"text":"Supernatural phenomena or entities are those beyond the laws of nature. The term is derived from Medieval Latin supernaturalis, from Latin super- 'above, beyond, outside of' + natura 'nature'. Although the corollary term \"nature\" has had multiple meanings since the ancient world, the term \"supernatural\" emerged in the Middle Ages and did not exist in the ancient world. Many cultures around the world lack concepts or reject distinctions between the natural and supernatural."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supernatural"},{"title":"Supernatural (American TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Supernatural is an American dark fantasy television series created by Eric Kripke. It was first broadcast on The WB and later The CW for 15 seasons from September 13, 2005, to November 19, 2020. The series follows brothers Sam and Dean Winchester as they hunt demons, monsters, and other supernatural beings. As the series unfolds, they battle angels and demons to protect the world and stop the Apocalypse. Themes include found family, brotherly codependency, Americana, psychological trauma, and Judeo-Christian mythology. Guest stars such as Misha Collins, Mark A. Sheppard, and Mark Pellegrino were promoted to series regulars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supernatural_(American_TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Saint_Pierre_tentant_de_marcher_sur_les_eaux_by_Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher.jpg/330px-Saint_Pierre_tentant_de_marcher_sur_les_eaux_by_Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Saint_Pierre_tentant_de_marcher_sur_les_eaux_by_Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher.jpg/330px-Saint_Pierre_tentant_de_marcher_sur_les_eaux_by_Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Saint Peter Attempting to Walk on Water (1766), painting by François Boucher","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaint_Pierre_tentant_de_marcher_sur_les_eaux_by_Fran%C3%A7ois_Boucher.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg/500px-GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg/1280px-GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg/500px-GuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Archangel Michael wears a late Roman military cloak and cuirass in this 17th-century depiction by Guido Reni.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuidoReni_MichaelDefeatsSatan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bernhard_Plockhorst_-_Schutzengel.jpg/500px-Bernhard_Plockhorst_-_Schutzengel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bernhard_Plockhorst_-_Schutzengel.jpg/500px-Bernhard_Plockhorst_-_Schutzengel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Schutzengel (English: \"Guardian Angel\") by Bernhard Plockhorst depicts a guardian angel watching over two children.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABernhard_Plockhorst_-_Schutzengel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Gati_or_existences.jpg/500px-Gati_or_existences.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Gati_or_existences.jpg/500px-Gati_or_existences.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In Jainism, a soul travels to any one of the four states of existence after death depending on its karmas.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGati_or_existences.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/San_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg/250px-San_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/94/San_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/San_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg/250px-San_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The patron saint of air travelers, aviators, astronauts, people with a mental handicap, test takers and poor students is Saint Joseph of Cupertino, who is said to have been gifted with supernatural flight.[84]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASan_Giuseppe_di_Copertino_18th_century_engraving.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Theodor_von_Holst_Bertalda_Assailed_Spirits.png/500px-Theodor_von_Holst_Bertalda_Assailed_Spirits.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa